import json
C=[]
def claim(claim,source,ind,cls,status,lim): C.append(dict(claim=claim,source=source,independent_verification=ind,**{'class':cls},status=status,limitation=lim))
IF='Independently verified fact'; RR='Reproduced result with limited independent verification'; IC='Internal consistency only'; MD='Method-dependent result'; IA='Inferred association'; UN='Unresolved'; NT='Not testable with available data'
claim('41,421 fills in the source','M1_REPORT; manifest','[RAW] csv.reader over Trades_GKOHNP140.csv: 41,421 rows x 167 columns, 0 validation failures (side, qty>0, price on 5-paise grid, qty multiple of lot, ts monotone non-decreasing); engine fills equal raw on 8 fields for all rows (compare_ref_vs_engine.py)',IF,'VERIFIED','All rows are accepted; none are excluded (is_duplicate flagged 0; no identical rows; trade ids differ in every same-key group). Raw column map verified by inspection, not against vendor documentation.')
claim('Parent-order count 39,874','M2B_RECONCILIATION_REPORT (parents.tsv rows)','[RAW] 39,874 distinct values of column 163; each maps to exactly one side, instrument, requested qty and app key. Column 4 (order number) has 37,258 distinct values and is reused across parents (2,224 order numbers map to >1 col-163 ids, 2,222 across instruments).',MD,'VERIFIED (count) / definition is a choice','Parent = column 163 (UniqueOrderIdentifier). Alternative key column 4 gives 37,258 but is demonstrably not a unique order identity. Not decided here.')
claim('23,684 opening allocations / 17,760 closing portions / 2,667 episodes','M2B_REPORT','[RAW]+[IMPL] independent re-implementation on raw rows: OA 23,684 (sum 1,414,545 units), CP 17,760 (sum 1,377,065), episodes 2,667; exact row-by-row match of OA (23,684/23,684), CP (17,760/17,760), episodes (2,667/2,667), lifecycle events (41,444/41,444), per-fill roles (41,421/41,421) against engine outputs',MD,'VERIFIED under src tie order','All counts are conditional on the same-second tie order (file order). Under trade-id or order-number tie order OA=23,682 and reversal fills=21 (see D-A01).')
claim('23 reversal fills, 26 mixed parents (23 with a reversal + 3 multi-fill without)','M2B_REPORT','[IMPL] ref: 23 split fills; 26 MIXED parents of which 23 contain a reversal fill and 3 do not',MD,'VERIFIED under src tie order','Reversal count is 20-23 under other tie orders.')
claim('15,889 of 17,760 closing portions are FIFO-vs-LIFO convention-sensitive','M2B_RECONCILIATION_REPORT','[IMPL] independent FIFO and LIFO allocation maps: 15,889 CPs whose {source OA: qty} map differs; identical set to engine',MD,'VERIFIED','Descriptive; depends on the definition (map of OA->qty differs).')
claim('Observed layer identical across FIFO/LIFO/AVG','M2B_REPORT','[IMPL] in the reference itself: OA, CP, lifecycle, episodes identical for the 3 conventions (observed layer has no convention input by construction); engine guard + byte comparison of C++ files also identical',IF,'VERIFIED','By construction the decomposition uses only net signed inventory; this is a structural property, not an empirical finding.')
claim('Reproduces TP-01 totals (opened 1,414,545 / closed 1,377,065 / remaining 37,480; realized FIFO 2,100,552.00 / LIFO 2,096,874.50 / AVG 2,100,111.63 rupees)','M1/M2B reports','[IMPL]+[RAW] my reference vs TP-01 position_episodes (2,667 exact per method), reconstructed_position_ledger pieces (FIFO 25,023 and LIFO 24,948 pieces equal as sorted (close_row, open_row, qty, pnl paise); AVG per-close max diff 3.6e-11 rupees), fill_roles (0 mismatches x 3 methods), reconciliation_summary realized',RR,'VERIFIED','TP-01 is an earlier implementation of the same matching rule by the same project: agreement is reproduction, not economic validation.')
claim('P&L is integer paise = (exit-entry)*qty*direction, no hidden multiplier; price paise, qty = units','SCHEMAS.md; M2C_UNIT_AUDIT','[RAW] FIFO realized from raw rupee price text with Decimal and no paise: 2,100,552.00 rupees; x100 equals reference integer paise 210,055,200 exactly; NIFTY qty gcd 65 (min 65), SENSEX gcd 20 (min 20)',IF,'VERIFIED for FIFO/LIFO','AVG is fractional paise (exact total 210,011,162.714...), stored as float; lot sizes 65/20 are data-derived multiples, not an exchange source.')
claim('Remaining inventory 37,480 units, all EXPIRED_UNCLOSED (81 instruments); no settlement P&L inferred','M1/M2B reports','[RAW]+[IMPL] 81 instruments non-flat at end (71 long, 10 short), 37,480 abs units; realized equals sum of closing allocations only (engine CA total == reference CA total); code inspection: no settlement field or valuation in pe/ (grep)',IC,'VERIFIED (units, no settlement P&L) / label is inferential','The label asserts the position was held to expiry from the absence of closing fills; for 27 of 81 the last fill is the day BEFORE expiry day, 13 last fills are at/after 15:30 IST. No settlement/exercise data exist.')
claim('Python and C++ outputs are byte-identical','M1/M2B reports','[XLANG] scratch-built C++ vs Python on raw-derived TSV (my own events file, not the TP-01 parquet): 5 lineage files + dump + roles byte-identical for 3 conventions x 3 tie orders (9 cases x 7 files, 0 diffs); fresh fuzz 400 sequences x 3 ties x 3 methods = 3,600 cases 0 byte diffs',IC,'VERIFIED','Cross-language consistency of a port; it is not historical/economic validation. C++ and Python were written by the same author with the same structure.')
claim('Independent reference agrees with C++ and Python on random sequences','M2B_REPORT (differential tests)','[IMPL] fuzz_diff.py: 400 random sequences (40,802 fills, 2,791 reversals, 15,206 partial reductions, 4,866 same-second mixed-side groups, 892 flagged duplicates), 3,600 cases: 0 mismatches C++ vs reference, 0 Python vs reference',RR,'VERIFIED','Generator is mine; covers prices on 5-paise grid and bounded sizes, not int64 overflow.')
